      "message": "I had to read this a few times (Might be good to improve the documentation with this as well): This appears to map a value within a range (eg, 0.5 in [0, 1]) to scale to some output range (eg, 1.5 in [1, 2] or 2 in [1, 3])) (Also note there is no clamping of the input value: x \u003d 0, range \u003d [5, 10] is apparently valid.\n\nIf we think of this spatially (since this is used in the UI), then the 0 case happens with something like x \u003d 5 range \u003d [5, 5] out range [10, 20], then zero doesn\u0027t make sense as a value.\n\nInstead I propose returning `out_min`, `out_max`, or `(out_min + out_max) / 2`.\n\nI also suggest clamping x in the return value with something like `androidx.core.MathUtils.clamp(x, out_min, out_max)`",
